    "text": "Caching: > When a server asks for a mapping from another server and receives the response, it stores this information in its cache memory before sending it to the client. > Ifthe same or another client asks for the same mapping, it can check its cache memory( server marks the response as unauthoritative )and solve the problem. Problems: lf a server caches a mapping for a long time, it may send an outdated mapping to the client. To counter this, the authoritative server adds TTL to the mapping.",
